  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Safety, Mitigate Conflict Risks and Disaster Risk Management in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the programme is to improve protection, safety and security and enhance access to justice and peaceful coexistence between refugees and host communities in eight camps in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, with particular attention to vulnerable groups such as youth, women, elderly, people with disabilities. The programme will provide a forum through which refugees and host communities will have improved access to protection services and conflict resolution mechanisms, as well as access to legal assistance and victim support services. The expected results will reinforce the capacities of actors that are currently working on community safety and security, justice and protection in both refugee and host communities, focusing on addressing crime, promoting women&#x2019;s empowerment, and preventing and responding to gender-based violence in a more inclusive and sustainable manner in accordance with national legal and local administrative structures and refugee protection standards.</narrative>
  </description>
